  SoftwareHelp_L("Zenkaku and Hankaku")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L(Chr(34) + "Zen" + Chr(34) + " means whole, " + Chr(34) + "han" + Chr(34) + " means " + Chr(34) + "half" + Chr(34) + ", " + Chr(34) + "kaku" + Chr(34) + " stands for " + Chr(34) + "square" + Chr(34) + " in Japanese. In MSX or in any word processing related with computers, hankaku is an adjective to describe 1-byte characters (English alphabets, numbers, western punctuation, unaccented katakanas, Japanese punctuation, Japanese accents; MSX supports unaccented hiraganas, unlike PC) while zenkaku, " + Chr(34) + "2-byte" + Chr(34) + " characters, include all hiraganas and katakanas, both accented and unaccented, English alphabets, special pictograms like large circles and measurement terms, Greek and Russian fonts, and thousands of kanjis.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("ZenkakuAndHankaku.htm", "MSX-BASIC - Referencia")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## DIR")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("DIR [/H] [/W] [/P] [compound-filespec]")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Displays the names of files on disk.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("The  compound-filespec specifies which files are to  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	listed.  If  the /H option is given,  then hidden files will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	also be listed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     In  the DIR command,  unlike all other commands,  it is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	permissible  to not give the main filename or  the  filename")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	extension,  and both will default to '*'. Thus a filename of")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	'FRED' is equivalent to 'FRED.*' and a filename of '.COM' is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	equivalent to '*.COM'.  Note that if the '.' at the end of a")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	main  filename is given,  then the extension is also assumed")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	to  have  been given,  so that the filename 'FRED.'  is  not")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	equivalent to 'FRED.*', unlike the example above.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     There are two formats of the listing.  If the /W option")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is  given,  then a 'wide' listing is printed,  with  several")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	filenames  output  per  line.   Sub-directory  names,   file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	attributes,  and the date and time each file was created are")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	not displayed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If  the /W option is not given,  then the filenames are")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	printed  with  one  filename per  line,  together  with  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	attributes, the file size and the date and time at which the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	file was last modified. The attributes are printed as an 'r'")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	if  the file is read-only and an 'h' if the file  is  hidden")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	(and  /H is given).  If the time of a file is zero (i.e. the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	file  does not have an associated time) then the time  field")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	will  not be printed.  If the date of a file is  zero,  then")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	neither  the date nor the time fields will be  printed.  The")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	formats  in which the dates and times are printed in can  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	changed (see HELP DATE and HELP TIME).")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  non-/W  display  is designed to fit  within  a  40")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	column screen,  but if fewer columns are available then some")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	fields  of the listing will not be shown so that the display")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	will  always fit on one line.  The number of files per  line")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	that  are  printed  when /W is specified  is  also  adjusted")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	according  to the screen width.  If the width of the display")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is less than 13 characters however,  then in both cases  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	filenames will wrap to the next line.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     At the top of the list of files, the volume name of the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	disk  and  the  name  of  the  directory  being  listed   is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	displayed.  At the bottom,  the number of files listed,  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	total  number  of  bytes  in the files  and  the  amount  of")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	remaining disk space is printed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     When  the directory of a sub-directory is printed,  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	first   two  items  listed  will  always  be   two   special")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	sub-directories called '.' and '..'. These are automatically")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	created  when  a new directory is created,  and it is  these")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	that allow '.' and '..' to be given in path names to signify")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  current and parent directories respectively  (see  HELP")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	SYNTAX for a description of paths).")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     When  printing  a  number  of  bytes,   the  number  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	truncated  and  printed as the number of kilobytes if 1K  or")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	greater.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If the /P option is given,  then the output will  pause")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	at the bottom of the screen until a key is pressed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DIR")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  filenames  and  directory  names  in  the  current")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directory of the current drive will be printed.  This  might")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	be as follows:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	      Volume in drive A: is MSX-DOS 2")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	      Directory of A:\")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     MSXDOS2  SYS r    4096 86-06-19  2:45p")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     COMMAND2 COM r   10496 86-06-19  2:46p")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     UTILS           <dir>  86-06-19  2:50p")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     HELP            <dir>  86-06-19  2:50p")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	      14K in 2 files   222K free")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The   disk  thus  contains  the  two  MSX-DOS  system  files")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	MSXDOS2.SYS and COMMAND2.COM,  which are read only,  and two")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directories called UTILS and HELP.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DIR B:\HELP/W")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     A  'wide'  directory format has been requested  of  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	HELP directory on drive B:. This might be as follows:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	      Volume in drive B: is MSX-DOS 2")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	      Directory of B:\HELP")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     BUFFERS .HLP    ATTRIB  .HLP    ASSIGN  .HLP")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     ATDIR   .HLP    CHDIR   .HLP    CD      .HLP")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     SYNTAX  .HLP    ENV     .HLP    BATCH   .HLP")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     EDITING .HLP")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	      25K in 10 files   222K free")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DIR  UTILS + HELP/P")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     This will list all the files in the UTILS directory and")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	all  the files in the HELP directory,  and will pause at the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	end of every screen full.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DIR .COM")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     No main filename was given,  and so defaults to *. Thus")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	this command is equivalent to the command DIR *.COM.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DIR COMMAND2")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     No extension was given,  so this defaults to  .*.  Thus")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	this command is equivalent to the command DIR COMMAND2.*.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("DIR", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## COPY")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("COPY [/H] [/P] [/A] [/B] [/V] [/T] source dest")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Copies data from files/devices to other files/devices.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("The definition of the source is:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("		  compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  compound-filespec specifies the files or  devices  that")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	are  to be copied.  If /H is given then hidden files may  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	copied.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The definition of the dest is:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("		  [d:][path][filename] | device")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	where d: and path default to the current drive and directory")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	respectively.  If any part of the filename is ambiguous then")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  appropriate  character  from  the  source  filename  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	substituted,  thus  allowing the files to be renamed in  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	process.  If  the  filename is not given,  then  the  entire")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	source  filename  is used.  If the dest  is  an  unambiguous")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directory,  then  the  files are copied into that  directory")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	with a filename of *.*.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     COPY  will  read as many source files as possible  into")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	memory before writing any out. When it can read no more into")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	memory (eg.  when it has used all available memory) it  will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	write out each file in the order that it read them.  When it")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	creates  each destination file,  it prints the source  file-")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	name.  Then  if it is unable to create the destination file,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	an error message is printed and the copy operation continues")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	with the next file. /P can be given to make the output pause")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	at the end of the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     Many  reasons exist for COPY to be unable to create the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	destination,  such as a read-only file already existing with")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  same  name.  Sometimes COPY will refuse to  create  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	destination  because the user may have made a  mistake.  For")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	example,  a  file cannot be copied onto itself,  or  several")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	files  cannot  be copied onto one  file.  A  'Cannot  create")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	destination'  error  may be given if the destination of  one")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	file  would delete a previous source file or a file  already")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	being used for something else (eg.  the currently  executing")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	batch file).  A 'Cannot overwrite previous destination file'")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	error  results  if an attempt is made to copy many files  to")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	one file.  This usually means that the intended  destination")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	was a directory, but that the name has been misspelled.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If  /A is specified,  then an ASCII copy is  performed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	This means that source files will only be read as far as the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	first   end-of-file   character  (CTRL-Z)  and   then   each")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	destination   will  have  a  single  end-of-file   character")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	appended to it.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     It is also possible to give a /A to the destination  or")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	to any of the filespecs in the compound-filespec separately,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	in  which  case  it  applies only to  that  source  or  dest")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	specification. Also /B may be given to reverse the effect of")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	/A.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  /V option can be given to turn write  verification")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	on  for  the  duration of the COPY command (see  the  VERIFY")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	command). This will ensure that data is written correctly to")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	disks but will slow the operation down.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     Normally, the destination files are given the same date")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	and time as the source files.  However, the /T option can be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	given  to  cause the destination files to have  the  current")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	date  and time.  The destination files will not be hidden or")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	read-only, regardless of the attributes of the source files.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The ATTRIB command can be used to change these.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If COPY gives a 'Not enough memory' error then probably")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	reducing the number of buffers (see the BUFFERS command)  or")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	removing some environment items (see HELP ENV on Environment")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Items) will free up sufficient memory.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     Note  that the COPY command is simpler than that in MS-")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DOS  and  MSX-DOS  1 because  it  cannot  concatenate  (join")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	together) files.  To do this,  a CONCAT command is available")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	(see the CONCAT command).")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	COPY FILE1 B:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  file FILE1 is copied from the current directory of")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the current drive to the current directory of drive B:.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	COPY /H  MSXDOS2.SYS + COMMAND2.COM  B:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  two hidden files MSXDOS2.SYS and COMMAND2.COM  are")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	copied to drive B:, thus making it a booting disk.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	COPY A:\DIR1 B:\DIR1 /V")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All files in the directory DIR1 from the root of  drive")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	A: are copied to a similar directory on drive B: with verify")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	on to ensure that the files were written correctly.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	COPY B:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files  in the current directory of  drive  B:  are")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	copied to the current directory of the current drive.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	COPY /A AUX CON")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     Characters  are read from the device AUX (which may  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	used for RS232 serial for example) to the device CON,  which")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is the screen.  The copy is done as far as the first end-of-")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	file  character.  If /A was not given,  then there may  have")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	been  no way of stopping the COPY operation without pressing")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the CTRL-STOP key.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	COPY A:*.DOC B:/T")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files  matching  *.DOC  (for  example   FILE1.DOC,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	FILE2.DOC and FILE3.DOC) are copied to the current directory")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	of drive B:  and are given the current date and time instead")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	of the dates and times of the *.DOC files.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	COPY *.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	AUTOEXEC.BAT -- File cannot be copied onto itself")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REBOOT.BAT -- File cannot be copied onto itself")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     This command told COPY to copy all files matching *.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	(in  this case AUTOEXEC.BAT and REBOOT.BAT) from the current")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directory of the current drive to the same place,  and  COPY")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	printed  the messages to warn of this.  No data in this case")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	was actually copied.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	COPY *.BAT DIR2")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	AUTOEXEC.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REBOOT.BAT -- Cannot overwrite previous destination file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     This command told COPY to copy all files matching *.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	(in  this case AUTOEXEC.BAT and REBOOT.BAT) to  a  directory")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	called DIR2.  DIR2,  however,  did not exist so AUTOEXEC.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	was  copied to a file called DIR2,  and then an attempt  was")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	made  to  copy REBOOT.BAT also to a file  called  DIR2.  The")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	message was printed as a warning that a mistake was probably")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	made  (in this case DIR2 not existing).  REBOOT.BAT was  not")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	actually copied anywhere.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("COPY", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## TYPE")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("TYPE [/H] [/P] [/B] compound-filespec | device")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Displays data from a file or device.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  compound-filespec specifies the files that are  to")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	be displayed, and /H allows hidden files to be typed. If the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	compound-filespec is ambiguous, then the filename is printed")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	before each one is typed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If  /B is specified,  then data is read from each  file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	and displayed without modification on the screen,  until the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	end of file is reached.  This may have strange effect on the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	screen if the file contains control characters.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If /B is not given, then TYPE will look for the end-of-")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	file  character  (CTRL-Z) and stop when it  finds  it.  Also")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	control characters except carriage return, line feed and tab")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	will be converted into a '^' symbol followed by that control")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	letter so that they will be visible on the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If /P is given,  then the output will pause at the  end")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	of the screen until a key is pressed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	TYPE FILE1")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     Data  is read from the file and printed on the  screen,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	up to the first end-of-file character.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	TYPE *.BAT/H/P")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All batch files, including hidden ones, are read in and")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	displayed.  A  prompt is printed at the end of every  screen")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	full.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	TYPE AUTOEXEC.BAT + REBOOT.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The files AUTOEXEC.BAT and REBOOT.BAT are displayed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	TYPE /B DIR1")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files  in the directory DIR1 are  printed  on  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	screen  and  no  interpretation is put on the  data  in  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	files.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	TYPE AUX")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     Data  is  read from the AUX device (which may  be,  for")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	example, an RS232 serial device) up to the first end-of-file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	character and printed on the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("TYPE", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## REN")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("RENAME [/H] [/P] compound-filespec filename")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("REN [/H] [/P] compound-filespec filename")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Renames one or more files.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  compound-filespec specifies the files that are  to")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	be renamed, and /H allows hidden files to be included in the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	rename operation.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  second  filename specifies the new  name  for  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	files.   A   '?'   in  the  new  name  indicates  that   the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	corresponding character from the filename being renamed will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	be used,  thus allowing an ambiguous rename. Thus '*' in the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	second  filename,  which is just equivalent to a  series  of")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	'?'s,  indicates that the whole of the filename or extension")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	will remain unchanged.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If  for some reason a particular file cannot be renamed")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	(eg.  if  a  file  or directory with the  new  name  already")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	exists)  then the offending filename will be  printed  along")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	with an error message and the rename operation will continue")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	with the next file. If many errors occur, then /P will cause")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the output to pause at the end of the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	RENAME FILE1 FILE2")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  file FILE1 in the current directory of the current")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	drive is renamed to FILE2.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REN B:\DIR1\*.DOC/H/P *.OLD")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	FILE2.DOC -- File exists")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files matching *.DOC in the directory called  DIR1")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	in the root directory of drive B:,  including hidden  files,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	are renamed with the same main name but with an extension of")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	.OLD.  The file FILE2.DOC could not be renamed because there")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	was already a file called FILE2.OLD in the directory, so the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	error  was  printed.  Neither  FILE2.DOC nor  FILE2.OLD  was")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	altered at all. If many such errors had been printed, then a")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	prompt would have been printed at the bottom of every screen")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	full.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REN DOC + FILE1 *.OLD")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files  in the directory called DOC  and  the  file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	FILE1,  both  in the current directory of the current drive,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	and renamed with an extension of .OLD.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("REN", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## DEL")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("DEL [/H] [/P] compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("ERA [/H] [/P] compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("ERASE [/H] [/P] compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Deletes one or more files.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  compound-filespec specifies which files are to  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted.  The  /H  option  allows hidden files  to  also  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     During  the  delete  operation,  if a  file  cannot  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted for some reason (eg.  it is set to 'read only') then")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  offending  filename  is printed  along  with  an  error")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	message,  and  the delete operation continues with the  next")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	file.  If  many such errors occur,  then the /P option  will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	cause the output to pause at the end of the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If the filename is *.*, then the prompt:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("		  Erase all files (Y/N) ?")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is  printed,  and  a reply is waited for.  If the  reply  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	anything other than 'Y' or 'y',  then the file deletion does")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	not take place. This is a safety feature designed to prevent")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	accidental loss of all files in a directory.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If files are deleted unintentionally on a disk that was")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	formatted  under  MSX-DOS 2,  then the UNDEL command may  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	used immediately afterwards to restore them again.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	ERASE FILE1.BAK")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The   file  FILE1.BAK  is  deleted  from  the   current")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directory of the current drive.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL *.COM/H")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files matching *.COM,  both hidden and not hidden,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	are deleted.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL B:\UTIL\*.COM + B:\UTIL\*.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All files matching *.COM or *.BAT are deleted from  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directory called UTIL on drive B:.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL B:\UTIL")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Erase all files (Y/N)?")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All files in the directory called UTIL on drive B:  are")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted.  Since so many files are being deleted, a prompt is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	printed first to prevent a catastrophe.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL *.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	AUTOEXEC.BAT -- Read only file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REBOOT.BAT -- Read only file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files  matching  *.BAT  are  deleted  except   for")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	AUTOEXEC.BAT  and REBOOT.BAT which have been marked as  read")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	only.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("DEL", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## DATE")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("DATE [date]")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Displays or sets the current date.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	If the date is given after the command,  then the  date")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is set to this value (for the format see below). If the date")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is  not  given after the command,  then the current day  and")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	date is printed and the new date is prompted for and  input.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	If  no  input  is given (i.e. if the 'enter'  key  alone  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	pressed) then the current date is not altered. Otherwise the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	input  is  assumed to be a new date,  and is interpreted  as")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	described  below.  If  the  date is invalid  then  an  error")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	message is displayed and the new date again prompted for and")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	input.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The date is expected to consist of up to three numbers,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	separated by one of the following characters:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     space tab , - . / :")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	with  spaces  allowed  either side  of  the  character.  Any")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	missing  numbers  will default to the current  setting.  The")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	year may either be a full century and year,  or may be  just")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  year  in which case the century defaults to 19  if  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	year is greater than 80 or 20 otherwise.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  format  in which the date is printed and input  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	flexible and can be changed. An environment item called DATE")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is set up by default to a format that is appropriate for the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	country  of  origin  of the MSX machine  (see  HELP  ENV  on")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Environment  Items).  For example,  on Japanese machines the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	default setting is YY-MM-DD.  The command SET DATE  DD-MM-YY")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	will  change  the date format to the UK format.  The  format")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	also affects the dates printed by the DIR command.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If  the DATE environment item is defined,  then it will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	be  printed  by the DATE command to indicate the  format  in")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	which the date is required to be input.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DATE 86-6-18")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The current date is set to the 18th June 1986.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DATE")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Current date is Wed 1986-06-18")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Enter new date (yy-mm-dd): - -19")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     No  parameter  was given,  so the current date of  18th")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	June  1986 was printed and a new date prompted for.  In  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	reply to the prompt, the date was updated to the next day by")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	only specifying the 19th.  Since the year and month were not")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	given, they remained the same.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	SET DATE = DD/MM/YY")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The date format has been changed to the UK format.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DATE")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Current date is Thu 19-06-1986")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Enter new date (DD/MM/YY):")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     No  parameter was given,  so the current date  of  19th")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	June  1986  was  printed in the UK format,  and  the  prompt")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	printed. The reply is expected in the UK format.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("DATE", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## TIME")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("TIME [time]")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Displays or sets the current time.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	If  the time is given after the command,  then the time")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is set to this value (for the format see below). If the time")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is  not given after the command,  then the current  time  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	printed  and the new time is prompted for and input.  If  no")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	input  is  given (i.e. if the 'enter' key alone is  pressed)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	then the current time is not altered. Otherwise the input is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	assumed  to be a new time,  and is interpreted as  described")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	below.  If  the  time is invalid then an  error  message  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	displayed and the new time again prompted for and input.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  time is expected to consist of up to four numbers,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	separated by one of the following characters:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     space tab , - . / :")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	with  spaces  allowed  either side  of  the  character.  Any")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	missing  numbers will default to the  current  setting.  The")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	first  number is the hour,  the second is the  minutes,  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	third is the seconds and the forth is the centi-seconds. The")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	centi-seconds  are not printed however since it is not  very")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	useful to know the current value,  or indeed to enter a  new")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	one.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The format in which the time is printed is flexible and")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	can   be  changed.   An  environment item (see  HELP ENV  on")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Environment  Items) called TIME is set up by default to  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	value '12', which indicates that the time will be printed in")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	12  hour format with a following 'a' or 'p' for am  and  pm.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The command SET TIME 24 will cause the time to be printed in")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	24 hour mode.  The time can be input unambiguously in either")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	format.  The  time format also affects the times printed  by")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the DIR command.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	TIME 16:45")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The current time is set to 4:45 pm.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	TIME")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Current time is 10:45:58a")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Enter new time:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     No  parameters  were  given,  so the  current  time  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	printed   (in this case in 12 hour mode) and  the  new  time")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	prompted for.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	TIME 10-50-30-23")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The time is set to 30.23 seconds after 10:50 am.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("TIME", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## RENAME")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("RENAME [/H] [/P] compound-filespec filename")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("REN [/H] [/P] compound-filespec filename")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Renames one or more files.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  compound-filespec specifies the files that are  to")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	be renamed, and /H allows hidden files to be included in the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	rename operation.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  second  filename specifies the new  name  for  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	files.   A   '?'   in  the  new  name  indicates  that   the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	corresponding character from the filename being renamed will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	be used,  thus allowing an ambiguous rename. Thus '*' in the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	second  filename,  which is just equivalent to a  series  of")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	'?'s,  indicates that the whole of the filename or extension")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	will remain unchanged.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If  for some reason a particular file cannot be renamed")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	(eg.  if  a  file  or directory with the  new  name  already")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	exists)  then the offending filename will be  printed  along")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	with an error message and the rename operation will continue")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	with the next file. If many errors occur, then /P will cause")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the output to pause at the end of the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	RENAME FILE1 FILE2")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  file FILE1 in the current directory of the current")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	drive is renamed to FILE2.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REN B:\DIR1\*.DOC/H/P *.OLD")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	FILE2.DOC -- File exists")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files matching *.DOC in the directory called  DIR1")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	in the root directory of drive B:,  including hidden  files,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	are renamed with the same main name but with an extension of")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	.OLD.  The file FILE2.DOC could not be renamed because there")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	was already a file called FILE2.OLD in the directory, so the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	error  was  printed.  Neither  FILE2.DOC nor  FILE2.OLD  was")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	altered at all. If many such errors had been printed, then a")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	prompt would have been printed at the bottom of every screen")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	full.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REN DOC + FILE1 *.OLD")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files  in the directory called DOC  and  the  file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	FILE1,  both  in the current directory of the current drive,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	and renamed with an extension of .OLD.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("RENAME", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## ERA")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("DEL [/H] [/P] compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("ERA [/H] [/P] compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("ERASE [/H] [/P] compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Deletes one or more files.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  compound-filespec specifies which files are to  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted.  The  /H  option  allows hidden files  to  also  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     During  the  delete  operation,  if a  file  cannot  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted for some reason (eg.  it is set to 'read only') then")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  offending  filename  is printed  along  with  an  error")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	message,  and  the delete operation continues with the  next")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	file.  If  many such errors occur,  then the /P option  will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	cause the output to pause at the end of the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If the filename is *.*, then the prompt:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("		  Erase all files (Y/N) ?")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is  printed,  and  a reply is waited for.  If the  reply  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	anything other than 'Y' or 'y',  then the file deletion does")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	not take place. This is a safety feature designed to prevent")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	accidental loss of all files in a directory.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If files are deleted unintentionally on a disk that was")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	formatted  under  MSX-DOS 2,  then the UNDEL command may  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	used immediately afterwards to restore them again.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	ERASE FILE1.BAK")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The   file  FILE1.BAK  is  deleted  from  the   current")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directory of the current drive.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL *.COM/H")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files matching *.COM,  both hidden and not hidden,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	are deleted.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL B:\UTIL\*.COM + B:\UTIL\*.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All files matching *.COM or *.BAT are deleted from  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directory called UTIL on drive B:.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL B:\UTIL")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Erase all files (Y/N)?")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All files in the directory called UTIL on drive B:  are")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted.  Since so many files are being deleted, a prompt is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	printed first to prevent a catastrophe.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL *.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	AUTOEXEC.BAT -- Read only file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REBOOT.BAT -- Read only file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files  matching  *.BAT  are  deleted  except   for")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	AUTOEXEC.BAT  and REBOOT.BAT which have been marked as  read")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	only.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("ERA", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## ERASE")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("DEL [/H] [/P] compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("ERA [/H] [/P] compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("ERASE [/H] [/P] compound-filespec")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Deletes one or more files.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  compound-filespec specifies which files are to  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted.  The  /H  option  allows hidden files  to  also  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     During  the  delete  operation,  if a  file  cannot  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted for some reason (eg.  it is set to 'read only') then")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  offending  filename  is printed  along  with  an  error")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	message,  and  the delete operation continues with the  next")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	file.  If  many such errors occur,  then the /P option  will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	cause the output to pause at the end of the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If the filename is *.*, then the prompt:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("		  Erase all files (Y/N) ?")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	is  printed,  and  a reply is waited for.  If the  reply  is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	anything other than 'Y' or 'y',  then the file deletion does")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	not take place. This is a safety feature designed to prevent")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	accidental loss of all files in a directory.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If files are deleted unintentionally on a disk that was")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	formatted  under  MSX-DOS 2,  then the UNDEL command may  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	used immediately afterwards to restore them again.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	ERASE FILE1.BAK")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The   file  FILE1.BAK  is  deleted  from  the   current")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directory of the current drive.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL *.COM/H")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files matching *.COM,  both hidden and not hidden,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	are deleted.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL B:\UTIL\*.COM + B:\UTIL\*.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All files matching *.COM or *.BAT are deleted from  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	directory called UTIL on drive B:.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL B:\UTIL")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Erase all files (Y/N)?")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All files in the directory called UTIL on drive B:  are")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	deleted.  Since so many files are being deleted, a prompt is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	printed first to prevent a catastrophe.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	DEL *.BAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	AUTOEXEC.BAT -- Read only file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REBOOT.BAT -- Read only file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     All  files  matching  *.BAT  are  deleted  except   for")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	AUTOEXEC.BAT  and REBOOT.BAT which have been marked as  read")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	only.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("ERASE", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## PAUSE")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("PAUSE [comment]")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Prompts and waits for a key press in a batch file.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  comments  consists  of an  arbitrary  sequence  of")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	characters.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  comment,  if  given,  is printed followed  by  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	prompt 'Press any key to continue... ' on the next line. The")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	system  will then wait for a key to be pressed and will echo")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  key  pressed  if it is a  printable  character.  If  no")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	comment is given as a parameter,  then just the prompt  will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	be printed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  main use of this command is to issue prompts  from")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	within a batch file.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	PAUSE")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Press any key to continue...")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     No comment was given, so just the prompt was printed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	PAUSE Insert document disk in drive B:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Insert document disk in drive B:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Press any key to continue")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  comment  given was 'Insert document disk in  drive")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	B:' so this was printed followed by the prompt.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("PAUSE", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## REM")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("REM [comment]")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Introduces a comment in a batch file.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  comment  is simply ignored,  and the next  command")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	executed.   The  comment  consists  of  a  sequence  of  any")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	characters  up to the maximum length of a command line  (127")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	characters).")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REM This is my AUTOEXEC batch file")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     This command,  either in a batch file or typed in, does")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	nothing at all with it's parameters.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("REM", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## VERIFY")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("VERIFY [ON | OFF]")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Displays/sets the current disk write verify state.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	If  no parameters are given,  then the  current  verify")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	state is displayed on the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     If ON or OFF is given, then the verify state is changed")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	appropriately.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  verify state affects all writes to disk.  If  OFF,")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the default state,  then data is simply written. If ON, then")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	after writing the data it is read back and compared with the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	original to ensure that it was written correctly.  The extra")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	overhead of this means that writing is slower when verify is")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	on.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	VERIFY")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	VERIFY=OFF")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     No   parameters  were  given,   so  the  current verify")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	state is printed, which in this case is off.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	VERIFY ON")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     Disk write verification is turned on.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("VERIFY", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## MODE")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("MODE number")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Changes the number of characters/line on the screen.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("The number must be in the range 1 to 80 inclusive,  and")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  number of characters per line on the screen will be set")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	to this.  The screen will be cleared and the cursor moved to")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the top left corner in the process.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	MODE 80")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  screen is set to 80 column mode and is cleared  in")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the process.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("MODE", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## BASIC")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("BASIC [program]")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Transfers control to MSX disk BASIC.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Program is the name of a BASIC program on disk.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     Control is passed to the built-in MSX BASIC, which will")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	load  and execute the BASIC program if specified.  If a  RAM")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	disk has been set up, then it can still be used from BASIC.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  BASIC  command _SYSTEM(" + Chr(34) + "command" + Chr(34) + ") can be  used  to")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	return to MSX-DOS,  and the optional command,  which can  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	any command mentioned in this manual,  will be executed.  If")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	the  command  is  not  given,   then  a  batch  file  called")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	REBOOT.BAT  will be  searched  for  and  executed  (see HELP")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	BATCH on Batch Files).")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	BASIC")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     MSX disk BASIC is entered.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	BASIC MYPROG.BAS")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     MSX  disk  BASIC  is entered,  and  the  BASIC  program")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	MYPROG.BAS loaded and RUN.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("BASIC", "MSX-DOS")

  SoftwareHelp_Begin()
  SoftwareHelp_L("## FORMAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("(MSX-DOS)")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Formato:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("FORMAT [d:]")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Finalidade:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("Formats (initializes) a disk.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Uso:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The  specified or default drive is formatted,  and  all")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	data on the disk will be destroyed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     After  giving  a  FORMAT  command,  an  option  may  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	prompted for, allowing the required format of the disk to be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	selected.  The exact nature of these prompts depends on  the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	manufacturer of the MSX machine.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     After formatting, there will be no files or directories")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	on  the disk,  and the maximum amount of disk space will  be")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	free. The disk will not have a volume name, but can be given")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	one with the VOL command.  To turn the disk into a boot disk")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	so  that  MSX-DOS  can  be started up  from  it,  the  files")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	MSXDOS2.SYS and COMMAND2.COM must be copied onto it with the")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	COPY command.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("**Exemplos:**")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	FORMAT B:")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	1 - Single sided")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	2 - Double sided")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	? 2")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	All data on drive B: will be destroyed")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	Press any key to continue...")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     The  command was given to format the disk in drive  B:.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	In  this case,  the options available were to select  either")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	double sided or single sided, and double sided was selected.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	The standard warning prompt was then printed.")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	FORMAT")
  SoftwareHelp_L("")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	     This  will  format the current drive after the  prompts")
  SoftwareHelp_L("	given above.")
  SoftwareHelp_Commit("FORMAT", "MSX-DOS")

